.TH MYNA-CONFIG 1 "2026-09-11" "myna-config" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
myna-config \- settings and onboarding for Myna dictation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B myna-config
.RI [ OPTION ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Myna Settings configures the Myna dictation service: it installs the myna
snap and a speech backend snap, connects the backend, binds the dictation
shortcut and edits the dictation settings the daemon reads live. With no
option it opens the settings window, or the onboarding wizard when dictation
is not yet set up.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-apply\-plan " JSON"
Run a backend apply plan as root. Used internally through
.BR pkexec (1);
not for interactive use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/snap/myna/common/.config/glib-2.0/settings/keyfile
The settings store shared with the myna snap.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snap (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
